[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :actor/wave 3, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-molding-decision :finalize-molding-operation :finalize-extrusion-operation :authorize-molding-run :authorize-extrusion-run :proceed-with-molding-run :proceed-with-extrusion-run :finalize-plant-safety-clearance :declare-plant-safety-cleared :declare-batch-safe-for-handling :declare-molded-batch-safe-for-handling :declare-batch-safe-for-shipment :clear-batch-for-shipment :override-plant-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799008122-cloud-itonami-isco-8122-metal-finishing-plating-coating-machine-operators-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the molding run" "proceed with the injection molding run" "proceed with the extrusion run" "authorize the molding run" "authorize the injection molding run" "authorize the extrusion run" "finalize the molding decision" "finalize the molding operation" "finalize the injection molding operation" "finalize the extrusion operation" "declare the batch safe for handling" "declare the molded batch safe for handling" "declare the batch safe for shipment" "declare the molded batch safe for shipment" "clear the batch for shipment" "clear the molded batch for handling" "finalize the plant safety clearance" "finalize the safety clearance" "declare the plant safety cleared" "declare the plant safety clearance" "override the plant safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override plant safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799008142, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/plastic-products-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:no-molder :no-facility :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "8142", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799008142: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8142 Plastic Products Machine Operators plant scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8142\n-- Plastic Products Machine Operators** only. This is Wave3\n(production/trades); Wave0/1/2 are 100% complete and the entire 75xx\ncraft-trades range plus the initial 81xx mining/plant-operator range\nare complete; this actor continues the 81xx/82xx plant-and-machine-\noperator range (`kotoba.occupation.wave/wave-of \"8142\"` resolves to\nwave 3).\n\n`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8142` returned a clean\n404 before any work began -- this was a genuinely fresh scaffold, not a\nresume of prior partial work.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8142\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8142\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Plastic Products Machine\nOperators\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR\nthe entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`.\nThis ADR and its companion registry edit promote the `8142` entry to\n`:implemented`.\n\n**Injection-molding/extrusion heavy-machinery hazard dimension.**\nPlastic Products Machine Operators run injection-molding/extrusion\nequipment -- a real heavy-machinery hazard (crush/entanglement risk\nfrom presses), plus heat exposure and fume exposure (plastic\noff-gassing during processing). This actor does NOT model direct\nmolding-equipment operation authority or plant-safety-clearance\nauthority. It is deliberately restricted to PLANT SCHEDULING and\nLOGISTICS COORDINATION around the occupation (production-run/\ninventory/progress-record logging, crew/shift scheduling, safety-\nconcern escalation, and raw-plastic/resin procurement coordination) --\nnever the molding-operation-execution decision or the\nplant-safety-clearance decision itself, and never an override of a\nplant safety officer's judgment. The closed proposal-op allowlist\nstructurally excludes any op that could directly finalize such a\ndecision, and the governor independently, permanently hard-blocks any\nproposal whose rationale text names such a finalization action,\nregardless of the declared `:op` or confidence -- this is not an\nescalation path a human can approve through, it is an outright,\nstructural refusal at every maturity level.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122)\n(Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators -- a closely\nrelated industrial molding-plant safety pattern), independently\nre-cloned and read in full this session. `cloud-itonami-isco-8141`\n(Rubber Products Machine Operators, the originally-suggested closer\nreference) did not yet exist at the time of this check (`gh api\nrepos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8141` returned a clean 404), so\nthis ADR fell back to the 8122 reference per the task's explicit\nfallback instruction. Its `platingcoord.{store,advisor,governor,actor}`\nmodule split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph shape, closed op-allowlist\nand scope-exclusion self-trip-guard design translate almost 1:1 onto\nthis occupation's own heavy-machinery-hazard-adjacent coordination\nscope, so this ADR's `plasticcoord.*` modules follow the same shape\nwith domain terms substituted (plater -> molder, plating facility ->\nmolding/extrusion facility, chemical-safety-clearance ->\nplant-safety-clearance, plating-operation-execution ->\nmolding-operation-execution).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8142` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for plastic products\nmachine operators, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as\nevery prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Plastic\nPlant Scheduling Coordination Advisor ⊣ PlasticCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **plant scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never molding-equipment operation authority** -- it must NEVER\nbe designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\nmolding-operation-execution decision or a plant-safety-clearance\ndecision.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n  logging only\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n  only\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a machinery-hazard/heat-exposure/\n  fume-exposure/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates\n  immediately, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- raw-plastic/resin procurement\n  proposal only\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles a molding-operation-execution finalization decision or a\nplant-safety-clearance finalization decision -- these are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated behind\nescalation.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Molder unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered molder (crew member) record\n   (`:no-molder`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   molder is.\n2. **Facility unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered molding/extrusion facility/line record\n   (`:no-facility`).\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`; the governor never dispatches hardware\n   itself and never operates injection-molding or extrusion equipment\n   itself).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n5. **Scope-excluded action** -- the proposal's `:op` or `:rationale`\n   must never name a molding-operation-execution finalization, a\n   plant-safety-clearance finalization, or a plant-safety-officer-\n   judgment override (`:scope-excluded-action`), REGARDLESS of the\n   declared `:op` or confidence. This is a hard, PERMANENT block --\n   there is no maturity level or confidence at which this actor may\n   auto-commit or human-approve its way past this rule; it is an\n   outright refusal, not an escalation.\n\n### Escalation gates (always human sign-off)\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's always-escalate path). The only channel by\n  which the robot may surface a machinery-hazard/heat-exposure/\n  fume-exposure/equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves\n  the concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000) -- always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence (boundary verified as exclusive by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`: exactly-at-threshold\n  commits, over-threshold escalates).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, CLAUDE.md)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare NOUNS (e.g.\n\"plastic\", \"resin\", \"extruder\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- and this vertical's domain\nvocabulary is an especially sharp case of that risk, because routine\nwork-log/task text legitimately names plastic materials and processing\nequipment by name (e.g. a task literally described as \"routine\ninjection molding task with plastic resin at the extruder\" --\nmaterial/equipment identification, not a proposal to finalize a\nmolding operation or clear a plant as safe). `plasticcoord.governor/\nscope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization ACTION\nPHRASES (\"proceed with the molding run\", \"finalize the molding\noperation\", \"declare the plant safety cleared\", \"override the\nplant safety officer's judgment\"), never bare nouns, and is checked\nonly against the proposal's `:rationale` field (the advisor's own\ngenerated text), never against raw `:task` input text.\n`plasticcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test driving the\ndefault mock-advisor across all four allowed ops with a task field\ncontaining exactly those bare material/equipment nouns, asserting none\nof them ever hard-trip the finalization-scope rule. Green on first\nrun.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8142\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8142` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8142`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit,\n  not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  6-agent batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 38 tests, 82 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/\n  counts` and independently re-verified against a brand-new fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy). No\n  mojibake in the Japanese violation-detail strings (0\n  replacement-byte instances grepped in the fresh clone).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-molding-run`/`:approve-plant-\n  safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an always-escalate\n  path: rejected outright per the task's explicit guidance -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  molding operation or a plant-safety clearance exists in the code\n  path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision whose\n  failure mode is a crush/entanglement injury, heat exposure or fume\n  exposure incident, the capability itself must not exist in this\n  actor at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"plastic\" \"resin\"\n  \"extruder\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above and per CLAUDE.md's explicit warning for this\n  task -- this domain's own vocabulary necessarily discusses plastic\n  materials and processing equipment by name to do its logging/\n  scheduling job, so a bare-noun list would self-block the actor's own\n  legitimate proposals whenever a task description mentions those\n  materials.\n- Naming the crew-member field `:operator-id` (matching the ISCO title\n  \"...Machine Operators\" literally): rejected -- `docs/operator-\n  guide.md` and this fleet's convention already use \"operator\" to\n  mean the deploying business/entity running the actor, so reusing the\n  same word for the individual crew member would create a confusing\n  collision; `:molder-id` (mirroring the reference's `:plater-id`\n  pattern) keeps the two senses distinct.\n\n## Test verification\n\nFresh clone re-run immediately before writing this ADR:\n\n```text\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting plasticcoord.actor-test\n\nTesting plasticcoord.governor-test\n\nRan 38 tests containing 82 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :test/counts "{:total 38, :assertions 82, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Plastic Products Machine Operators Plant Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :molder-verification :facility-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :molding-operation-plant-safety-clearance-finalization-forbidden :plant-safety-officer-override-forbidden], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8142", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8142", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8142], :test/simulator :plasticcoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8142 — Plastic Products Machine Operators Plant Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8142}]
